  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The density of a sphere is measured by measuring the mass and diameter. If it is known that the maximum percentage errors in the measurement of mass and diameter are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;respectively then the maximum percentage error in the measurement of density is&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "11",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The density can be computed by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8733;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the percentage error in measurement of density is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
}